lunduke-city (0.9-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A failed save no longer collects an open tax year, and Quit stays in
    the city when Save fails. The error dialog includes the path and the
    operating-system reason.
  * Enable disasters is stored in the city file and restored on load,
    including the Options check. A paused city loads paused.
  * Tax, funding, and saved options count as unsaved changes.
  * The budget window shows this year's tax, the balance Close will post,
    and the funding a broke city can actually pay. Closing a menu budget
    applies those percents to road, police, and fire maintenance.
  * A tool that cannot build says why and does not mark the city unsaved.
    A bridge says it costs $50. The cash-flow graph uses the real dollars.
  * A repeated notice returns to the message bar. Scenario win and loss
    pause the city and open a dialog. The side panel scrolls, and the
    window will not shrink small enough to clip the tools. Menu letters
    no longer collide. A name that is only spaces is rejected.

 -- LCOS <lcos@lunduke.com>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

lunduke-city (0.9-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Graphs and Evaluation use the last finished census, so phase 0 no
    longer flashes a population of zero. Evaluation preview restores
    every field it writes and does not advance the simulator RNG.
  * The tax-year budget pauses the city. Saving collects that year.
    New City resets road, police, and fire funding to 100%. Closing
    the budget cannot spend the city negative, and Cancel restores
    the rates from when the window opened.
  * Generator-default islands honor rivers, lakes, and trees. "No
    trees" plants nothing.
  * Quit, closing the window, New City, Load, and Play Scenario ask
    Save, Discard, or Cancel when the city has unsaved changes.
  * Save confirms the path after the .cty suffix, writes a temporary
    file, and replaces the destination with rename. Symlinks are not
    followed. A failed scenario load keeps the current city. A seed
    that is not a whole number stays on the land page.
  * Cash flow and total population no longer wrap in 16 bits. Loaded
    city names drop controls and bidi marks. Sound files are size
    capped, and the mixer queue is bounded. Zoom starts below the
    maximum, Slow and Medium slow sprites, and Space pauses the map.

 -- LCOS <lcos@lunduke.com>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 19:10:00 +0000

lunduke-city (0.9-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Residential demand keeps the residential ratio. Industrial demand is
    clamped to its own maximum.
  * Disaster messages play their sounds. Options → Auto-goto is on for a
    new city and follows the flag stored in a save.
  * The city map keeps its image and redraws tiles that changed, including
    the unpowered-zone blink. The tool outline is separate. Paused cities
    do not animate tiles. The minimap keeps one color buffer, a 6:5 shape,
    and redraws only the viewport when the view scrolls.
  * Tool drags grab the pointer and scroll at the edge of the view.
  * Loading a city clears a previous error and reports "Loaded a saved
    city."
  * Evaluation refreshes opinion and problems on a month of game time.
    Graph legends show residential, commercial, and industrial as people,
    and crime and pollution as levels.
  * Power, crime, and pollution maps keep a retained image. Density maps
    draw 60 by 50 cells. Sounds are decoded once and mixed on one stream.
  * Closing the query dialog restores the tool hint. The earthquake
    outline stays on the shaken tiles. Modal dialogs pause the simulation
    and show a waiting budget when they return.

 -- LCOS <lcos@lunduke.com>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 06:30:00 +0000

